    "Scouting Notes": "Multi Inning Reliever\n Delivery: hybrid windup with a high leg kick, stretch is a more abbreviated leg kick\n Very low slot on the pitch, I'd guess under 20 degrees on the arm angle\n Two seam is a really good pitch, bordering on a plus pitch for him, though I'd like to see it commanded better\n Two different breakers are both fine/fringe average offerings that can play better at times, but lack consistency\n I like the way the changeup can play off the two seam, average or a bit better pitch in that context\n There is a cutter thrown in the 86 88 range that I don't mind either.\n The two seam carries the repertoire, but the other stuff is good enough to play\n Command in the zone is a big part of his issue at times this year, but there is a relief arm in here if he can improve the consistency and general command",
